@theme notgood
// Writer-commons, themes batch. From content/arcs/outlines.md, "The struggle themes". Any department, either shift.
// Fill-ins assumed: {home} a place ("Lisk"), {family} with "my" ("my gran"), {hobby} an activity ("painting"),
// {since} a length of time ("five years"). A beat that names one lists it in needs:, so people without it skip it.

== beat 1
tone: light
duty: true
hint: Hang on. Let me check that. Again. One more time.
mem: checking
them: Sorry. I'm checking it again. I know I checked it. I'm checking that I checked it.   [laugh]
them: It's fine. It was fine the first three times. I just like to be sure.
? choice
* Want me to look? Fresh eyes.   flavour:practical mem:freshEyes
  them: Would you? Then I can stop. Probably.
* It's perfect. I can tell from here.   flavour:cheer
  them: From there? You can't even see it. ...Thank you, though.   [laugh]
them: Right. Done. Definitely done. Mostly.

== beat 2
tone: heartfelt
hint: Got a minute? There's something I still think about. Stupid, really.
mem: mistake
them: When I was new, I made a mistake. Small. Nobody got hurt. It got fixed the same day.   [sigh]
them: But I still think about it. At night. I check everything twice because of it.
them: I keep thinking someone will notice I'm not as good as they think.
? choice
* Everyone makes one of those. It's how you learn the job.   flavour:listen mem:everyone
  them: That's what they said at the time. I didn't believe them. Maybe I'm starting to.
* I've seen your work. You're good. Really good.   flavour:cheer mem:good
  them: You have to say that. Do you? You don't, do you. Huh.
  + them: You don't say things you don't mean. I've noticed. So... thanks. I'll try to hear that.
* Tell me what happened. Then it's out.   flavour:share mem:told
  them: All right. It's very boring. That's the funny thing. It's very, very boring.   [laugh]
them: Sorry. That came out bigger than I meant. Thanks for listening.

== beat 3
tone: resolution
hint: You'll never guess what {boss} said to me. Sit down. I'm still sitting down.
mem: fine
them: I told {boss} about the old mistake. I don't know why. It just came out.
them: And they said, "That? I'd forgotten that. You've been one of the steady ones since."
them: Forgotten. All this time. And they'd forgotten.   [laugh]
? choice
* Told you.   flavour:cheer
  them: You did. I'm going to stop checking twice. Once and a half. Let's start there.
* How does it feel?   flavour:listen mem:feels
  them: Lighter. Like putting down a bag I didn't know I was carrying.
  + them: Lighter. And a bit silly. Mostly lighter. You helped. You know you did.
them: Right. One check. One. Watch me.
